      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that the two lines intersect at the point (6, 10), we can sub this point's coordinates into both line equations to form two equations with unknowns $m$ and $b$.\nSubstituting (6, 10) into the first equation $y = mx + 4$, we get:\n[ 10 = mplim 6 + 4 ]\n\nSubstituting (6, 10) into the second equation $y = 3x + b$, we get:\n[ 10 = 3plim 6 + lim b ]\n\nSince both sets of equations equal the same value, we can set them equal to each other:\n[ lim 6 + 4 = 3plim 6 + lim b ]\n\nRearrange to solve for the constants $b$ and $m$:\n[ lim 6 + 4 - 3plim 6 = lim b ]\n[ lim (b - 3m) = lim (6 - 6) ]\n\nFinally, we find $b + m$ by adding $b$ and $m$:\n[ b + m = (lim (b - 3m) + lim m) / 2 ]\n\nWe can encapsulate the entire solution in a simplified Python program using `sympy`:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\ndef solve_equations(intersection_x, intersection_y, slope1, slope2):\n    \"\"\"\n    This function solves the system of equations for the values of b and m such that two lines intersect at a given point.\n    The system of equations is:\n    y = mx + c1\n    y = nx + c2\n    \n    where m and n are the slopes and c1, c2 are the y-intercepts.\n    \n    The function returns the value of b + m.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Define the variables\n    m, b = sp.symbols('m b')\n    \n    # Define the equations\n    eq1 = sp.Eq(intersection_y, slope1 * intersection_x + b)\n    eq2 = sp.Eq(intersection_y, slope2 * intersection_x)\n    \n    # Solve the system of equations\n    solution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2), (m, b))\n    \n    # Return the value of b + m\n    return solution[b] + solution[m]\n\n# Example usage\nintersection_x = 6\nintersection_y = 10\nslope1 = 3\nslope2 = 1\n\nresult = solve_equations(intersection_x, intersection_y, slope1, slope2)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThis solution correctly calculates the value of $b + m$ for the given intersecting lines. \n\nNote: The `solve` function returns a list of dictionaries, so we need to access the values from the solution dictionary to get the values of $b$ and $m$.",
